From: degas maintainer <mikhail@advnirr.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hidl/audio: drop the duplicate mediatek audio service

Upstream hardware/mediatek added android.hardware.audio.service.mediatek, which
degas already ships from device/xiaomi/degas/audio with the boot-crash fix
(MtkAudio.h/SoundTriggerHw.h), soundtrigger3 V3 and vendor.mediatek.hardware.audio-impl.
Having the module in both namespaces makes soong fail:
  module "android.hardware.audio.service.mediatek" found in multiple namespaces
  (device/xiaomi/degas and hardware/mediatek) when including in vendor partition.
device.mk installs ours, so drop upstream's definition. Nothing in hardware/mediatek
references it by name.

diff --git a/hidl/audio/Android.bp b/hidl/audio/Android.bp
index fd9c220..81e18e7 100644
--- a/hidl/audio/Android.bp
+++ b/hidl/audio/Android.bp
@@ -3,30 +3,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 //
 
-cc_binary {
-    name: "android.hardware.audio.service.mediatek",
-
-    init_rc: ["android.hardware.audio.service.mediatek.rc"],
-    relative_install_path: "hw",
-    vendor: true,
-
-    srcs: ["service.cpp"],
-
-    cflags: [
-        "-Wall",
-        "-Wextra",
-        "-Werror",
-    ],
-
-    shared_libs: [
-        "libcutils",
-        "libbinder",
-        "libbinder_ndk",
-        "libhidlbase",
-        "liblog",
-        "libutils",
-        "libhardware",
-        "android.hardware.soundtrigger3-V1-ndk",
-        "vendor.mediatek.hardware.audio-V1-ndk",
-    ],
-}
+// NOTE (degas): the "android.hardware.audio.service.mediatek" cc_binary that
+// upstream added here is intentionally dropped. degas ships its own service in
+// device/xiaomi/degas/audio with the boot-crash fix (MtkAudio.h/SoundTriggerHw.h),
+// soundtrigger3 V3 and vendor.mediatek.hardware.audio-impl. Keeping both makes
+// soong fail with "found in multiple namespaces". device.mk installs ours.
